# Chained kans: open kan -> replacement draw -> closed kan (owed dora + new dora order)
# (engine.md §4.1, §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5 item 10).
# Seat 0 discards 5z -> Seat 1 calls daiminkan on 5z (owes kan dora #1: 1p -> dora 2p).
# Seat 1 draws rinshan[0] (4th 9m) and declares ankan 9m!
# Per engine.md §4.2: owed dora (1p) flips BEFORE ankan, then ankan, then new dora (7p -> dora 8p),
# then rinshan[1] (7s).
# Seat 1 wins by Rinshan Kaihou tsumo on 7s, counting BOTH kan dora (one 2p + two 8p = 3 dora)!
# Scoring for Seat 1 (non-dealer, South):
#   Hand: 234p 56s 88p + daiminkan 5555z + ankan 9999m + tsumo 7s
#   Yaku: rinshan (1) + yakuhai_haku (1) + dora:3 (2p, 8p, 8p) = 5 han (Mangan)
#   Fu: 20 base + 2 tsumo + 16 open kan(5z) + 32 closed kan(9m) = 70 fu
#   Non-dealer Mangan tsumo: 2000 / 4000 (+8000).

[meta]
name: open_kan_to_closed_kan_chain
title: Open kan -> replacement draw -> closed kan reveals owed dora then ankan then new dora
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5.10
unverified: rules.md §5 item 10 (Mahjong Soul chained kan dora order)

